<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<CustomField xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        This comment must stay INSIDE the root <CustomField> element - a comment placed ABOVE the
        root breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with "unable to find matching parent xml
        file". The formula below is UNCHANGED by this note; this is documentation only.

        🔴 KNOWN CONSEQUENCE OF THE 2026-08-16 ACQUISITION NDA SEQUENCE REVERSAL - RECORDED, NOT
        FIXED. This formula (TODAY() - Date_Sent__c) was written when the acquisition sequence was
        Pending -> Sent -> Received -> Signed, with 'Sent' as a MIDDLE step - so it correctly
        counted days an NDA had been out awaiting signature. The sequence is now
        Pending -> Received -> Signed -> Sent, with 'Sent' as the TERMINAL step, so this same
        formula now counts days since the NDA was FINISHED, growing forever after completion
        rather than stopping. It is user-visible: Days_Out__c is a column on
        reports/Acquisitions/NDA_Tracker_Recent, so a completed NDA will read e.g. "out 340 days".

        This field is unchanged by the sequence-reversal change and the drift is intentionally
        left for a USER decision. Candidate remedies, named without choosing one:
          1. Re-point the formula at a future Date_Received__c field once one exists (see the
             companion gap noted in pathAssistants/NDA_Path_Acquisition's own 2026-08-16 comment
             and FSD §27.6) - would restore "days awaiting signature" as the meaning.
          2. Restrict the formula to non-terminal statuses (e.g. blank once Status__c = 'Sent' on
             an Acquisition_NDA row) - keeps the field but stops it from growing past completion.
          3. Retire this field for acquisition NDAs specifically, since disposition NDAs' own
             'Sent' is not terminal and are unaffected by this drift.
        Do not implement any of the three without an explicit decision from whoever owns this
        report/field.
    -->
    <fullName>Days_Out__c</fullName>
    <description>Days since the NDA was sent (TODAY - Date Sent). Gives the dashboard NDA Tracker table a numeric column and flags aging NDAs.</description>
    <externalId>false</externalId>
    <formula>IF(ISBLANK(Date_Sent__c), null, TODAY() - Date_Sent__c)</formula>
    <formulaTreatBlanksAs>BlankAsZero</formulaTreatBlanksAs>
    <label>Days Out</label>
    <precision>18</precision>
    <required>false</required>
    <scale>0</scale>
    <trackHistory>false</trackHistory>
    <trackTrending>false</trackTrending>
    <type>Number</type>
    <unique>false</unique>
</CustomField>
